{"about_the_game":"Frames work like every other door frame: you go through them and then you are somewhere else. The only difference is that with frames this &quot;somewhere else&quot; can be anywhere, <strong>discontinuities in space included</strong>. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/4667e87859fe69be7d12f956046e0713.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/4667e87859fe69be7d12f956046e0713.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/4667e87859fe69be7d12f956046e0713.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>If anywhere should be somewhere else frames can be <strong>move</strong>d. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/1a2715ef82400340dfeb5790d7dd9095.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/1a2715ef82400340dfeb5790d7dd9095.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/1a2715ef82400340dfeb5790d7dd9095.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>If something is in the right place, but with the wrong size frames can <strong>change the size</strong> of objects. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/9284035376283165e37dc58e1b2f97fe.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/9284035376283165e37dc58e1b2f97fe.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/9284035376283165e37dc58e1b2f97fe.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>And if something falls in an inconvenient direction frames can <strong>change gravity</strong> of objects. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/b8331b250a7d516cb9b859c4b0ec5448.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/b8331b250a7d516cb9b859c4b0ec5448.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/b8331b250a7d516cb9b859c4b0ec5448.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>And frames can do even more:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>The ubiquitous cubes and activation buttons. <br></li><li>A &quot;Paint Gun&quot; allows to dynamically open and close frames. <br></li><li>A &quot;Light Gun&quot; that changes how objects interact with frames. <br></li><li>Frames can have any size and appear in high numbers. <br></li><li>All features of frames are implemented in the most general way possible and cooperate with each other. No scripted events, no restrictive special cases. </li></ul><br>All this results in a staggering number of puzzle-possibilities and the carefully crafted levels make sure to use them to the fullest in this logic-based physics-puzzler.<br><br>Other features are:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>A story almost as complex as the game mechanics. <br></li><li>All mechanics are explained &quot;intuitively&quot; through level-design without the need of explicit tutorials or text. <br></li><li>95 levels (including free DLC). Every single level exploits a different aspect of the mechanics. No filler, no repitition. <br></li><li>A hint mechanic, so you never get stuck. <br></li><li>Full support for mouse/keyboard and controller with freely configurable inputs.</li></ul><br><strong>Thinking with portals is easy. Now, try thinking with frames. </strong>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1916610?t=1698094076","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/1916610?t=1698094076","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1698094076","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1698094076","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"Frames work like every other door frame: you go through them and then you are somewhere else. The only difference is that with frames this &quot;somewhere else&quot; can be anywhere, <strong>discontinuities in space included</strong>. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/4667e87859fe69be7d12f956046e0713.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/4667e87859fe69be7d12f956046e0713.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/4667e87859fe69be7d12f956046e0713.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>If anywhere should be somewhere else frames can be <strong>move</strong>d. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/1a2715ef82400340dfeb5790d7dd9095.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/1a2715ef82400340dfeb5790d7dd9095.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/1a2715ef82400340dfeb5790d7dd9095.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>If something is in the right place, but with the wrong size frames can <strong>change the size</strong> of objects. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/9284035376283165e37dc58e1b2f97fe.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/9284035376283165e37dc58e1b2f97fe.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/9284035376283165e37dc58e1b2f97fe.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>And if something falls in an inconvenient direction frames can <strong>change gravity</strong> of objects. <br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/b8331b250a7d516cb9b859c4b0ec5448.poster.avif?t=1698094076\" width=640 height=480 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/b8331b250a7d516cb9b859c4b0ec5448.webm?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/extras/b8331b250a7d516cb9b859c4b0ec5448.mp4?t=1698094076\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>And frames can do even more:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>The ubiquitous cubes and activation buttons. <br></li><li>A &quot;Paint Gun&quot; allows to dynamically open and close frames. <br></li><li>A &quot;Light Gun&quot; that changes how objects interact with frames. <br></li><li>Frames can have any size and appear in high numbers. <br></li><li>All features of frames are implemented in the most general way possible and cooperate with each other. No scripted events, no restrictive special cases. </li></ul><br>All this results in a staggering number of puzzle-possibilities and the carefully crafted levels make sure to use them to the fullest in this logic-based physics-puzzler.<br><br>Other features are:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>A story almost as complex as the game mechanics. <br></li><li>All mechanics are explained &quot;intuitively&quot; through level-design without the need of explicit tutorials or text. <br></li><li>95 levels (including free DLC). Every single level exploits a different aspect of the mechanics. No filler, no repitition. <br></li><li>A hint mechanic, so you never get stuck. <br></li><li>Full support for mouse/keyboard and controller with freely configurable inputs.</li></ul><br><strong>Thinking with portals is easy. Now, try thinking with frames. </strong>","developers":["MechanicsDriven"],"dlc":[2540190],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/1916610/header.jpg?t=1698094076","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended